From b78212cc0fbb99737ce89955c5d4e288ce257bfb Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: stephan-xyz <stephan@zehrer.xyz>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 10:41:02 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 30/31] dwc2d: find USB devices plugged in or removed after
 boot

Every second dwc2d asks the root port and every port of every hub for
connection changes. A new device is reset and enumerated, a hub with
everything behind it; a removed one is forgotten and its address reused.

A keyboard plugged in later is used if there is none. All network
adapters are kept, but only one receives: the network stack sees the
best by link (an RTL815x with a link, else the LAN7800, else an RTL815x
without a link, else CDC Ethernet) and is moved to another adapter when
one is plugged in or removed or the link of an RTL815x changes. The
adapter that takes over gets the MAC address the stack started with, so
the stack and its DHCP lease keep working. Adapters plugged in later do
not wait for their link; the rescan looks at it.

Without any adapter at boot, the scheme is still registered (as
network.usb, with the board's address), so an adapter plugged in later
works.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
